        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2524] The SA (eMSP) shall support calculation of the ECDHE secret and the key derivation function, as specified by NIST Special Publication 800-56A, for the encryption of private keys.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                167,
                1123,
                247
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    1123.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    1123.0,
                    247.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    247.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2525] The EVCC shall support calculation of the ECDHE secret and the key derivation function, as specified by NIST Special Publication 800-56A, for the decryption of encrypted information like private keys.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                268,
                1123,
                348
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    268.0
                ],
                [
                    1123.0,
                    268.0
                ],
                [
                    1123.0,
                    348.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    348.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2526] When the mechanism defined by [V2G20-2320] indicates usage of the (elliptic curve) EC as specified by [V2G20-2674], the SA (eMSP) shall generate a 521 bit ephemeral public/private key pair using elliptic curve secp521r1[SECG notation] as specified by NIST Special Publication 800-56A.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                370,
                1121,
                475
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    370.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    370.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    475.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    475.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2527] When the mechanism defined by [V2G20-2320] indicates usage of the curve corresponding to the signature algorithm specified by [V2G20-2319], the SA (eMSP) shall generate a 448 bit ephemeral public/private key pair using ECC algorithm X448 as specified by IETF RFC 7748.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                499,
                1121,
                605
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    137.0,
                    499.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    499.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    605.0
                ],
                [
                    137.0,
                    605.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2528] The private key generated by [V2G20-2526] or [V2G20-2527] shall be used by the SA (eMSP) as ephemeral private key for calculation of the session key as defined by [V2G20-2535].",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                626,
                1120,
                707
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    137.0,
                    626.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    626.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    707.0
                ],
                [
                    137.0,
                    707.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 2 It is assumed that the ephemeral private key is destroyed by the SA after the session key was derived.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                729,
                1105,
                755
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    137.0,
                    729.0
                ],
                [
                    1105.0,
                    729.0
                ],
                [
                    1105.0,
                    755.0
                ],
                [
                    137.0,
                    755.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2529] When the mechanism defined by [V2G20-2320] indicates usage of the (elliptic curve) EC as specified by [V2G20-2674], the \"Subject Public Key\" of the OEM provisioning certificate shall be used as static public key for calculation of the session key as defined by [V2G20-2535].",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                776,
                1121,
                882
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
